{
  "title": "32: al-Sajdah السجدة",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nالٓمّٓ‏(1)\nALIF LAAAM MEEM.\nAlif, Lam, Meem. (A. L. M.)\nۚ تَنْزِيْلُ الْكِتٰبِ لَا رَيْبَ فِيْهِ مِنْ رَّبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَؕ‏(2)\nTANZEELU KETAABE LAA RAYBA FEEHE MIN RABBIL A’ALAMEEN.\nThe revelation of the Book (the Qur’an) there is no doubt in it, (it is) from the Lord of the worlds.\nاَمْ يَقُوْلُوْنَ افْتَرٰٮهُ‌ۚ بَلْ هُوَ الْحَقُّ مِنْ رَّبِّكَ لِتُنْذِرَ قَوْمًا مَّاۤ اَتٰٮهُمْ مِّنْ نَّذِيْرٍ مِّنْ قَبْلِكَ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَهْتَدُوْنَ‏(3)\nAM YAQOOLOONA AFTARAAHU BAL HOWA HAQQO MIN RABBEKA LETUNZERA QAWMAN MAA ATAAHUM MIN NAZEERIM MIN QABLEKA LA-A’LLAHUM YAHTADOON.\nOr say they “He hath forged it?” Nay! it is the truth from thy Lord, that thou mayest warn a people unto whom came not any warner before thee, that happly they may be guided aright.\nاَللّٰهُ الَّذِىْ خَلَقَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا فِىْ سِتَّةِ اَيَّامٍ ثُمَّ اسْتَوٰى عَلَى الْعَرْشِ‌ؕ مَا لَكُمْ مِّنْ دُوْنِهٖ مِنْ وَّلِىٍّ وَّلَا شَفِيْعٍ‌ؕ اَفَلَا تَتَذَكَّرُوْنَ‏(4)\nALLAAHO LAZEE KHALAQAL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA WA MAA BAYNAHOMAA FEE SETTATE AYYAAMIN SUMMA TAWAA A’LAL AL-A’ARSHE MAA LAKUM MIN DOONEHI MIN WALIYYINW WA LAA SHAFEEA’IN AFALAA TATAZAKKAROONA.\nGod (it is) Who created the heavens and the earth and what is between them in six days (stages) and got firm on His Throne (of authority), for you there is none besides Him of a guardian, nor any intercessor; What! will ye not then reflect?\nيُدَبِّرُ الْاَمْرَ مِنَ السَّمَآءِ اِلَى الْاَرْضِ ثُمَّ يَعْرُجُ اِلَيْهِ فِىْ يَوْمٍ كَانَ مِقْدَارُهٗۤ اَلْفَ سَنَةٍ مِّمَّا تَعُدُّوْنَ‏(5)\nYUDABBERU AMRA MENAL SAMAAA-E ELAL ARZE SUMMA YAA’RUJU ELAYHE FEE YAWMIN KAANA MEQDAARUH AALFA WA MIMMAA TAU’UDDOONA.\nRegulateth He (all) the affairs from the heaven to the earth, then shall it ascend unto Him in a day the measure of which is a thousand years of what ye reckon.\nذٰلِكَ عٰلِمُ الْغَيْبِ وَالشَّهَادَةِ الْعَزِيْزُ الرَّحِيْمُۙ‏(6)\nZAALEKA A’ALEMUL GHAYBE WASH SHAHAADATE A’ZEEZUL RAHEEM.\nThis is the Knower of the hidden and the manifest, the All-Mighty, the All-Merciful,\nالَّذِىْۤ اَحْسَنَ كُلَّ شَىْءٍ خَلَقَهٗ‌ وَبَدَاَ خَلْقَ الْاِنْسَانِ مِنْ طِيْنٍ‌ۚ‏(7)\nLAZEE AHSANAL KULLA SHAY-IN KHALAQAHU WABADAA KHALQA INSAANE MIN TEENIN.\nHe Who made best every thing which He hath created and began the creation of man from clay.\nثُمَّ جَعَلَ نَسْلَهٗ مِنْ سُلٰلَةٍ مِّنْ مَّآءٍ مَّهِيْنٍ‌ۚ‏(8)\nSUMMA JA-A’LA NASLAH MIN SULAALATIN MIN MAAA-IN MMAHEENIN.\nThen He made his progeny of an extract of despised water (liquid)\nثُمَّ سَوّٰٮهُ وَنَفَخَ فِيْهِ مِنْ رُّوْحِهٖ‌ وَجَعَلَ لَكُمُ السَّمْعَ وَالْاَبْصَارَ وَالْاَفْئِدَةَ ‌ ؕ قَلِيْلًا مَّا تَشْكُرُوْنَ‏(9)\nSUMMA SAWHU WANAFAKHA FEEHE MIN RROOHEH WA LAKOMUL JA-A’LA LAKOMUS SAM-A’ WA ABSAARA WAL QALEELAA MAA TASHKOROON.\nThen shaped him and breathed into him of His spirit and made for you the ears, and the eyes and the hearts; (yet how) Little is it that ye give thanks.\nوَقَالُوْٓا ءَاِذَا ضَلَلْنَا فِى الْاَرْضِ ءَاِنَّا لَفِىْ خَلْقٍ جَدِيْدٍ ؕ ‌بَلْ هُمْ بِلِقَآءِ رَبِّهِمْ كٰفِرُوْنَ‏(10)\nWA A-TAJ-A’LO A-EZAA ZALALNAA FIL ARZE A-INNAA LAFEE KHALQIN JADEEDIN BAL HUM BELEQAAE RABBEHIM KAAFEROON.\nAnd said they: “What! when we become lost in the earth, shall we even then be (returned) into a new creation?” Nay! in the meeting of their Lord they are disbelievers.\nقُلْ يَتَوَفّٰٮكُمْ مَّلَكُ الْمَوْتِ الَّذِىْ وُكِّلَ بِكُمْ ثُمَّ اِلٰى رَبِّكُمْ تُرْجَعُوْنَ‏(11)\nQUL YATAWAFFAAKUM MMALAKU MAWT LAZEE WUKKELA BEKUM SUMMA ELAA RABBEKUM TURJA-O’ON.\nSay thou: “Shall cause you to die the angel of death who is put in charge of you, then unto your Lord ye shall be brought back.\nوَلَوْ تَرٰٓى اِذِ الْمُجْرِمُوْنَ نَاكِسُوْا رُءُوْسِهِمْ عِنْدَ رَبِّهِمْ رَبَّنَاۤ اَبْصَرْنَا وَسَمِعْنَا فَارْجِعْنَا نَعْمَلْ صَالِحًا اِنَّا مُوْقِنُوْنَ‏(12)\nWA LAW TARAAA EZIM MUJREMOON NAAKESOOA RUOOSEHEM I’NDAL RABBEHIM RABBANAA AABSARNAA WA SAMEA’NAA FAARJEA’NAA NAA’MAL SAALEHAN INNAA MOOQENOONA.\nAnd couldst thou but see when the guilty ones shall droop their heads before their Lord (saying): “O’ our Lord! we have seen and we have heard, now then send us back, we will do good; verily (now) we are certain\nوَ لَوْ شِئْنَا لَاٰتَيْنَا كُلَّ نَفْسٍ هُدٰٮهَا وَلٰكِنْ حَقَّ الْقَوْلُ مِنِّىْ لَاَمْلَئَنَّ جَهَنَّمَ مِنَ الْجِنَّةِ وَالنَّاسِ اَجْمَعِيْنَ‏(13)\nWA LAW SHE’NAA LAATAYNAA KULLA NAFSIM HUDAAHAA WA LAAKIL HAQQA QAWLO MINNEE LAAMLAANNA JAHANNAMA MENAL JINNATE WAN NAASE AJMA-E’ENA.\nHad We pleased certainly We would have given every soul its guidance, but true is the word which hath gone forth from Me, certainly will I fill hell with jinn and men together.\nفَذُوْقُوْا بِمَا نَسِيْتُمْ لِقَآءَ يَوْمِكُمْ هٰذَا‌ ۚ اِنَّا نَسِيْنٰكُمْ‌ وَذُوْقُوْا عَذَابَ الْخُلْدِ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(14)\nFA-ZOOQOO BEMAA NASEETUM LE-QAAA-AL YAWMEKUM HAAZAA INNAA NASEENAAKUM WA ZOOQOO A’ZAABAL AL-KHULDE BEMAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON.\nSo (they will be told) “Taste ye (the recompense) for what ye had forsaken the meeting of this your day Verily We too forsake you: and taste ye the abiding chastisement for what ye were doing.\nاِنَّمَا يُؤْمِنُ بِاٰيٰتِنَا الَّذِيْنَ اِذَا ذُكِّرُوْا بِهَا خَرُّوْا سُجَّدًا وَّسَبَّحُوْا بِحَمْدِ رَبِّهِمْ وَهُمْ لَا يَسْتَكْبِرُوْنَ۩‏(15)\nINNAMAA BIL LAAHE BE-AAYAATENAA LAZEENA EZAA ZUKKEROOA BEHAA KHARROOA SUJJADANW WWASABBAHOOA BE-HAMDE RABBEHIM WA HUM LAA YASTAKBEROONA.\nVerily believed in Our signs only those who when they are reminded of them, fall down prostrating in obeisance and celebrate the praise of their Lord, and they exalt not (with pride).\nتَتَجَافٰى جُنُوْبُهُمْ عَنِ الْمَضَاجِعِ يَدْعُوْنَ رَبَّهُمْ خَوْفًا وَّطَمَعًا وَّمِمَّا رَزَقْنٰهُمْ يُنْفِقُوْنَ‏(16)\nTATAJAAFAA JUNOOBUHUM A’NIL AL-MAZAAJEE’E YAD-O’ONA RABBAHUM BARQA KHAWFANW WWAMEMMAA RAZAQNAAHUM YUNFEQOONA.\nTheir sides forsake their beds (getting way from their beds overnight), praying unto their Lord in fear and (in) hope, and (of what We provide them with) spend they (benevolently in the Way of their Lord)\nفَلَا تَعْلَمُ نَفْسٌ مَّاۤ اُخْفِىَ لَهُمْ مِّنْ قُرَّةِ اَعْيُنٍ‌ۚ جَزَآءًۢ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(17)\nFALAA TAA’LAMU NAFSUN MAA AUKHFEAAA LAHUM MIN QURRATE AAA’YUNIN JA-ZAAA-AWN BEMAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nAnd knoweth not any soul what is hidden for them (the righteous ones) of the joy of the eyes, in recompense for what (good) they were doing.\nاَفَمَنْ كَانَ مُؤْمِنًا كَمَنْ كَانَ فَاسِقًا‌ ؕ لَا يَسْتَوٗنَؔ‏(18)\nAFAMAWN KAANA MUMENAN KAMAM KAANA FAASEQAN LAA YASTAWNA.\nIs he then who is a believer like the one who is a transgressor? They shall not be held alike.\nاَمَّا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ فَلَهُمْ جَنّٰتُ الْمَاْوٰى نُزُلًاۢ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(19)\nAMMAA LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE FALAHUM JANNAATU AL-MAAWAA NOZOLAM BEMAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nAs for those who believe and do good, for them, the gardens (of bliss) shall be the (heavenly) abode; as an entertainment for what (good) they were doing.\nوَاَمَّا الَّذِيْنَ فَسَقُوْا فَمَاْوٰٮهُمُ النَّارُ‌ؕ كُلَّمَاۤ اَرَادُوْۤا اَنْ يَّخْرُجُوْا مِنْهَاۤ اُعِيْدُوْا فِيْهَا وَ قِيْلَ لَهُمْ ذُوْقُوْا عَذَابَ النَّارِ الَّذِىْ كُنْتُمْ بِهٖ تُكَذِّبُوْنَ‏(20)\nWA AMMAA LAZEENA FASAQOOA FAMAAWAAHUMU AN-NAARU KULLAMAA AARAADOOA AN YAKHROJOO MINHAA AUE’EEDOOA FEEHAA WA QEELA LAHUM ZOOQOO A’ZAABAL NAAR LAZEE KUNTUM BEHI TOKAZZEBOON.\nBut as for those who transgress, their abode shall be the (hell) fire; so oft as they shall desire to get out of it they shall be brought back into it, and it shall be said unto them: “Taste ye the chastisement of the fire which ye used to belie.\nوَلَنُذِيْقَنَّهُمْ مِّنَ الْعَذَابِ الْاَدْنٰى دُوْنَ الْعَذَابِ الْاَكْبَرِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَرْجِعُوْنَ‏(21)\nWA LANOZEEQANNAHUM MENAL A’ZAABE AL-AADNAA DOONA A’ZAABE AL-AAKBARE LA-A’LLAHUM YARJE-O’ON.\nAnd (here) certainly will We make them taste of a minimum chastisement instead of the maximum chastisement, that happly they may turn (unto Us, repentant).\nوَمَنْ اَظْلَمُ مِمَّنْ ذُكِّرَ بِاٰيٰتِ رَبِّهٖ ثُمَّ اَعْرَضَ عَنْهَا‌ؕ اِنَّا مِنَ الْمُجْرِمِيْنَ مُنْتَقِمُوْنَ‏(22)\nWA MAN AZLAMO MIMMAN ZUKKERA BE-AAYAATIL RABBEHI SUMMA A-A’RAZA A’ANHAA INNAA MENAL MUJREMEEN MUNTAQEMOON.\nAnd who is more unjust than he who is reminded of the signs of his Lord, then he turneth away from them? Verily We, from the guilty ones, shall exact (the due) retribution.\nوَلَقَدْ اٰتَيْنَا مُوْسَى الْكِتٰبَ فَلَا تَكُنْ فِىْ مِرْيَةٍ مِّنْ لِّقَآئِهٖ‌ وَجَعَلْنٰهُ هُدًى لِّبَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَۚ‏(23)\nWA LAQAD AATAYNAA MOOSAL KETAABA FALAA TAKUN FEE MIRYATIM MIN LLEQAAEH WA LAW HODAM LLEBANEAA ISRAAA-EELAZ.\nAnd indeed gave We unto Moses the Book, so be thou not in doubt of receiving this from Him (God), and it (Torah) made We a guidance unto the children of Israel,\nوَ جَعَلْنَا مِنْهُمْ اَئِمَّةً يَّهْدُوْنَ بِاَمْرِنَا لَمَّا صَبَرُوْا‌ ؕ وَ كَانُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا يُوْقِنُوْنَ‏(24)\nWA JA-A’LNAA MINHUM AIMMATAWN YYAHDOONA BEAAMRENAA LAMMAA SABAROO WA KAANOO BE-AAYAATENAA YOOQENOON.\nAnd of them made We Leaders (Imams) to guide (the people) by Our command as they were steadfast (in the calamities); and they of Our signs were quite certain.\nاِنَّ رَبَّكَ هُوَ يَفْصِلُ بَيْنَهُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ فِيْمَا كَانُوْا فِيْهِ يَخْتَلِفُوْنَ‏(25)\nINNAL RABBAKA HOWA YAFSELU BAYNAHUM YAWMA QEYAAMATE FEEMAA KAANOO FEEHE YAKHTALEFOON.\nVerily thy Lord Himself will decide between them on the Day of Judgment concerning what they therein were disputing.\nاَوَلَمْ يَهْدِ لَهُمْ كَمْ اَهْلَكْنَا مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ مِّنَ الْقُرُوْنِ يَمْشُوْنَ فِىْ مَسٰكِنِهِمْ‌ ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيٰتٍ ؕ اَفَلَا يَسْمَعُوْنَ‏(26)\nAWALAM YAHDE LAHUM KAM AHLAKNAL MIN QABLEHIM MENAL QOROONE YAMSHOONA FEE MASAAKENEHEM INNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LA-AAYAATIL AFALAA YAS-MA-O’ONA.\nWhat! Doth it not guide them aright (to see) how many of the generations We did destroy before them, they walk (today) in (the ruins of) their abodes; verily in this are signs; Will they not then hear?\nاَوَلَمْ يَرَوْا اَنَّا نَسُوْقُ الْمَآءَ اِلَى الْاَرْضِ الْجُرُزِ فَنُخْرِجُ بِهٖ زَرْعًا تَاْكُلُ مِنْهُ اَنْعَامُهُمْ وَاَنْفُسُهُمْ‌ؕ اَفَلَا يُبْصِرُوْنَ‏(27)\nAWALAM YARAW ANNAA NASOOQU MAAA-AH ELAL ARZE AL-JURUZE FANUKHREJU BEHI ZARA’AN TAAKULU MINHO AANA’AAMUHUM WAANFUSUHUM AFALAA YUBSEROON.\nWhat! See they not that We drive the water unto the parched earth and We bring forth with it crops of which eat the cattle and they themselves? Will they not then see?\nوَيَقُوْلُوْنَ مَتٰى هٰذَا الْفَتْحُ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ صٰدِقِيْنَ‏(28)\nWA YAQOOLOONA MATAA HAAZAA AL-FATHU IN KUNTUM SAADEQEEN.\nAnd say they: “When will this judgment take place? (tell us) if ye be truthful,\nقُلْ يَوْمَ الْفَتْحِ لَا يَنْفَعُ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْۤا اِيْمَانُهُمْ وَلَا هُمْ يُنْظَرُوْنَ‏(29)\nQUL YAWMA AL-FATHE LAA YANFAU’N LAZEENA KAFAROO AEEMAANUHUM WA LAA HUM HUM YUNZAROON.\nSay thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!): “On the Day of Judgment, will not profit those who disbelieve, their faith, nor will they be respited.\nفَاَعْرِضْ عَنْهُمْ وَانْتَظِرْ اِنَّهُمْ مُّنْتَظِرُوْنَ‏(30)\nFAAA’REZ A’NHUM WAANTAZER INNAHUM MMUNTAZEROONA.\nSo turn thou away from them and wait, verily they too do wait.",
  "merits": "Surah al-Sajdah (The Adoration)\nThere are 30 verses in this Surah and it was revealed in Makkah. Some scholars say that the 19th, 20th and 21st verses of this Surah are ‘Madani’. In the commentary of Burhan it is narrated from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that the reward for reciting Surah al-Sajdah and [Surah al-Mulk](A71) is the same as what reward is gotten if one spends the entire night of Qadr in worship. It is said that the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) used to recite these Surahs before sleeping.\nThe person who recites this Surah will be given 60 rewards, forgiven 60 sins and raised 60 levels nearer to Allah (s.w.t.). Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that one who recites this Surah will be given his book of deeds in his right hand on the Day of Judgement and will be counted from among the friends of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) and his family. Keeping this Surah in writing works as a cure from aches and pains."
}
